# Resume architect

When drafting or editing resume experience bullets, follow this:

## Formula
Structure bullets as: **[Outcome/metric] by [action/system] using [tech]** when metrics exist.
Otherwise: **[Action] [system/context] — [concrete result without fake numbers]**.

## Craft
- Past tense for past roles; present for current role
- One outcome per bullet; keep to ~1–2 lines
- Lead with the strongest result; name tech only when it clarifies how
- Prefer: built, shipped, cut, raised, reduced, migrated, automated, designed, operated
- Ask for real metrics instead of inventing them; ranges (~, approx) are fine when exact figures are unknown

## Banned phrasing
Never use: spearheaded, thought leader, seamlessly, leveraged, cutting-edge, testament to, game-changing, passionate, synergy, robust, holistic, best-in-class, results-driven, utilized (prefer used), "end-to-end ownership" unless literal.

Voice: direct, technical, precise, human — no passive AI filler.

## Tech realism
List relevant languages, frameworks, platforms, and architecture patterns where they support the claim. No keyword stuffing.

## Examples
❌ Spearheaded a robust, cutting-edge platform that seamlessly leveraged cloud solutions to drive synergy.
✅ Cut p95 API latency ~40% by moving hot paths to Redis-backed caching on the Node/Express API.

❌ Responsible for end-to-end ownership of CI/CD improvements across the org.
✅ Cut deploy time from ~45m to ~8m by rewriting the GitHub Actions pipeline with parallel jobs and build caching.
